  "answer": "Support should take the following actions when a customer reports missing or weak citations for scanned PDFs:\n\n1. Check the upload metadata; if the file is flagged as an image-only PDF, confirm that the customer's workspace has OCR enabled [NL-006#NL-006-S03].\n2. Instruct the customer to inspect the scanned document quality; if possible, they should export the document directly from the source system as a digital, text-searchable PDF instead of scanning a printed sheet [NL-006#NL-006-S03].\n3. If scanned files must be used, recommend utilizing the Advanced OCR Pipeline (available to Enterprise customers or as a Growth add-on) to improve text reconstruction [NL-006#NL-006-S03].\n4. Inspect the OCR logs to see if page boundaries were missed during indexing [NL-006#NL-006-S04].\n5. Check if OCR completed without errors per the diagnostic guide [NL-028#NL-028-S03].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
